<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lombards</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Langobards, Longobards</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombards</a> were a Germanic people who migrated from the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pannonia">Pannonia</a> by the early 6th century. In 568, under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alboin">Alboin</a>, they invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and founded a kingdom centred on Pavia, with powerful duchies at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spoleto">Spoleto</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benevento">Benevento</a>, which lasted until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>'s conquest in 774. The region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a> keeps their name.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lombards.jpg" alt="Lombards" width="320" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johann Gustav Droysen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Italien_zur_Langobardenzeit.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
